# Drives the game camera through its commands: the sandbox camera is a retreat_engine_api
# GameCamera, and the engine builds the real camera from it.
# Run: cargo run -p retreat_sandbox -- --headless --commands scripts/verify/camera.cmds
# Expected pictures:
#   camera_default.png: the usual view: cube in the middle of the green plane, seen from above
#                       and to the left (identical to the first picture of any other script).
#   camera_moved.png:   the same scene seen corner-on from the front right and lower (camera at 6, 3, 6),
#                       the cube still in the middle.
#   camera_wide.png:    the same position with a 90 degree field of view: everything looks
#                       smaller and farther away, the plane fills less of the picture.

snapshot camera_default
camera.set_position sandbox_camera 6 3 6
camera.look_at sandbox_camera 0 0.5 0
wait 1
assert.position sandbox_camera 6 3 6
snapshot camera_moved
camera.set_fov sandbox_camera 90
wait 1
snapshot camera_wide
quit
